  "title": "Voynich Manuscript: The 600-Year-Old Book Nobody Can Read",
  "description": "The Voynich Manuscript is a 600-year-old book that nobody on Earth can read. Even America's top codebreakers tried, and failed. So what is it?\n\nThe Voynich Manuscript, kept at Yale's Beinecke Library, is filled with an unknown script, strange plants, star charts and bathing women. William Friedman's codebreaking team attacked it from 1944, and in 2009 radiocarbon dating put its vellum in the early 1400s, long before Wilfrid Voynich bought it in 1912. Its words even repeat in patterns, like a real language.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a true story like this every day. Do you think it is a secret code or a lost language? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #voynichmanuscript #unsolvedmysteries #stickstory",
